===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Zander}}, from {{der|en|sla}} a language, perhaps via {{der|en|gml|sandāt}}.<ref>{{R:Duden}}</ref> Pfeifer states that the first German attestation is in East Central German as ''czandas'' (in the ''Marienburger Treßlerbuch''<ref name="TDW"/>) circa 1400, which he derives from a supposed Old Pomeranian *''sądač'';<ref>{{cite-book|author=Wolfgang Pfeifer|title=Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen|edition=2 |publisher=Deutscher Taschenbuch Verlag|year=1995|ISBN=3-423-03358-4}}</ref> Low Prussian forms include ''Zand'' and other Slavic languages (e.g. Kashubian) have been considered as possible sources.<ref name="TDW">''Trübners deutsches Wörterbuch'' (1957), W-Z, page 322</ref> {{dbt|en|sandre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈzæn.də(ɹ)/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ændə(ɹ)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|zander}}

# A European freshwater fish in the family [[Percidae]], closely related to the [[perch]], {{m|mul|Sander lucioperca}}.
# Any fish of the genus {{m|mul|Sander}} that live in freshwater.

